{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the first came out.</b> Why did he come out first? So that he would go out with his impurities — meaning all the filth of blood. Rabbi Abbahu gave a parable: to a bathhouse attendant who enters first to flush out the bath, and afterward his master enters. Another interpretation: <b>And the first came out</b> — because he was destined to inherit this world, which is first. Another interpretation: <b>And the first came out</b> — because he was the last drop of Yitzhak, as Rabbi Yosi said to that matron: when two pearls are placed in a tube, the last one comes out first. So too Yaakov was the first drop, therefore he came out after Esav. Admoni — of the language of אדם, 'red' (rouge) in the vernacular." "<b>Admoni.</b> He was fully formed; Esav was hairy like a mantle of hair. And one should not interpret admoni as meaning reddish, for what does reddish have to do with a mantle of hair? And there are those who interpret it: he was entirely hair like a mantle, for the word aderet is not in construct state and not attached."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The acronym אאומי״ץ is expanded following its standard resolution as 'red' (rouge) in Old French (לע״ז); the exact spelling of the French gloss is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:54.913571259Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}